    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_316a86ee75d04f182ebdf99158be5cd7ff523a00b332d07807d1e43c97d70531",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For the first Hamiltonian's classical dynamics, the variational representative determines which classical symmetries become constraints on quantization. Multiplier-derived L_78 and L_13 carry specified five-generator Noether sets, whereas the Hamiltonian-derived L_S carries Gamma_4, Gamma_5, and Gamma_8; preserving these sets leads to distinct equations (27), (31), and (43), with the latter two reducing in moving coordinates to elementary temporal normal forms.",
