      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b1bab6e068c5c9d1ceefae8c7e5b554213e077c8833b7be2ad845e10b1ab4992",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The classical nonlinear equation and two symmetry-preserving parabolic equations expose the same linear structure in different representations. A symmetry-adapted point transformation sends the classical equation to a free particle, while moving spatial coordinates reduce the two parabolic equations to constant-coefficient temporal equations that the source matches to the b=-3 and b=-5/2 members of its classical linear family.",
