      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d0baa6246738dee8e9052abc9cbf7342607e00a7748ff547c7fc72d268da7fc7",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For a second-order equation, the source closes a construction chain: independent first integrals or nondegenerate Lie-symmetry selections determine Jacobi last multipliers; a multiplier transforms as a Jacobian-weighted density and is the velocity Hessian of a Lagrangian; integrating it twice therefore yields variational representatives. Different admissible symmetry pairs can consequently expose multiple Lagrangians for the same dynamics.",
