    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f75b0acedba032ab0a7ef9bcad980ad99e05cc4bdb2b45faa19bc86b9638c754",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Against the source's stated aim of obtaining a discrete quantum spectrum in the modified-xp program, the two symmetry-preserving quantum equations actually analyzed for the first model are both reported to have continuum spectra. Symmetry successfully organizes the two quantization branches, but within those branches it does not deliver the desired discrete Riemann-zero realization.",
